### What does that mean?
This diagnostic trouble code (DTC) is a generic 파워트레인 code, which means that it applies to OBD-II equipped vehicles. Brands of vehicles affected include but are not limited to Ford, Lexus, Chevy, BMW, Toyota, Jaguar, Acura, Volvo, Nissan, etc. Although generic, the specific repair steps may vary depending on make/model/엔진. Anecdotally this code seems more common in Ford & Chevy vehicles.
Every vehicle has a 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) or 엔진 제어 모듈(ECM) (파워트레인 / 엔진 제어 모듈). It''s basically the "brain" or main computer of the vehicle, it''s job is to 모니터링 a variety of 센서 readings and use that information to run the 엔진 in the most efficient operation given the 전류 conditions.
Basically this P0174 code means that the 상류(Upstream) 산소 센서 in 뱅크 2 reporting a 희박 condition 
(과도하게 much oxygen in the 배기). On V6/V8/V10/V12 engines, 뱅크 2 is the 측면 of the 엔진 that doesn''t have 실린더 #1.
The 엔진 uses what are called 산소 or oxygen sensors in the 배기 stream to determine the 공기 to 연료 비율 of the 배기 leaving the 엔진. The 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) (or 엔진 제어 모듈(ECM)) uses that information to determine how much 연료 to inject via the 연료 injectors many times per second. The ideal 공기:연료 비율 is 14.7:1. The 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) CAN 통신 adjust the amount of 연료 by adding more 연료 or taking away 연료 to keep the 엔진 operating efficiently and with 낮음 emissions.
If an 산소 센서 is telling the 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) through it''s reading that the 배기 has 과도하게 much 공기 in it, the 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) compensates by adding more 연료. In this case it''s adding more 연료 to 뱅크 2. The 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) will only adjust up to a certain point to the amount of 연료 that it will inject in an attempt to bring that 공기:연료 비율 as close to optimal as possible. When the 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) has reached it''s 한계 on how much 연료 it will inject but the 전방 (상류(Upstream)) 뱅크 2 산소 센서 still detects a 희박 condition, the 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) will continue to command a higher than normal amount of 연료 to 뱅크 2 and will trigger this code and illuminate the MIL (오작동 indicator lamp).
