변속기 제어 시스템 TCS 오작동
This diagnostic trouble code (DTC) is a generic 파워트레인 code, which means that it applies to OBD-II equipped vehicles. Although generic, the specific repair steps may vary depending on make/model.

### What does that mean?
Many vehicles have a 제어 모듈 for the 자동 변속기 called a 변속기 제어 모듈 (변속기 제어 모듈(TCM)). The 엔진 제어 모듈 (엔진 제어 모듈(ECM)) communicates with the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) to 모니터링 the 자동 변속기 for faults. If the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) detects a 결함 in the 자동 변속기 and sets a 변속기 related 결함 code, the 엔진 제어 모듈(ECM) is informed of this also and sets a P0700 in the 엔진 제어 모듈(ECM) memory.
This illuminates the 오작동 Indicator Lamp (MIL) to let the 드라이버 know there is a problem. If this code is present and the MIL (오작동 Indicator Lamp) is illuminated that basically means there is at least one 변속기 code set in the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM)''s memory. P0700 is an informational code only. It doesn''t point to a direct 결함 in the 엔진, only a general 결함 in the 변속기. More diagnosis is necessary to identify what the 변속기 결함 is. This requires a scan tool that will communicate with the 변속기 모듈.SymptomsSymptoms of a P0700 DTC may include:오작동 Indicator Lamp (MIL) illuminationThe 변속기 may exhibit drivability problems like slipping, etc.CausesMore often then not, the cause of this code is that there is a 변속기 problem of some kind. The 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) 감지됨 the problem and set a code. P0700 means that a 결함 code is stored in the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM). However this doesn''t rule out the possibility of a failed 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) or 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) (unlikely).Possible SolutionsFor a P0700 the only real solution is to acquire a scan tool that will communicate with the 변속기 제어 모듈. Extracting this code from the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) will be the first step in repairing the 결함 in the 변속기.If the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) compatible scan tool will not communicate with the 변속기 제어 모듈 then that is a good indication that there may be a 결함 with the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) itself.Related  DTC DiscussionsRegister now to ask a question (free)2005 Dodge Durango multiple codes set for tranny P0700, P0845, P0731, P0732, P0733I have a 2005 Dodge Durango SXT 4.7L with the 5-45RFE 변속기.  It has roughly 138,000 miles on it.  I recently replaced the 변속기 시프트 솔레노이드 pack after the truck went into "limp mode".  After replacing the 솔레노이드 pack I was able to clear the original trouble codes for the 솔레노이드...trans code P0700 2004 pt cruiser gt turboI have a 2004 cruiser gt turbo throwing the code P0700..indicates either a faulty 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM)...or 솔레노이드 problem in the trans (auto)..car has 144K two owner miles.in better than +9 condition.  When the weather drops 미만 50 degrees F   the trans does not go into 기어 until the car has warmed up for almo...2003 dodge caravan code p0700Awhile back my 2003 dodge caravan 엔진 점검등 light went on. Went to autozone to scan, p0700, p1698 and p0500. Van will not go 초과 50 unless I force accelerate. Changed the in and out 속도 센서 and a remanufactured 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) from ALL COMPUTER RESOURCES, inc. this 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) gave me more problems, All Comput...2006 Dodge Magnum p0700 and u0100 codesI own a 06 dodge magnum getting a p0700 and u0100 code. Car shuts off 10 times a day ive replaced cam and 크랭크샤프트 sensors, 퍼지 솔레노이드, plugs, 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM),and 파워트레인 제어 모듈(PCM) and still same stuff. It is a 5.7l rt hemi if anyone has had this problem help me........P0700, no additional codes?Hi all,
I feel almost guilty posting here; typically I''m very thankful for mechanics and grateful for the work they do. But I just moved to a new state and my jeep starting giving me trouble, so I took it to a local garage (a NAPA AutoCare center). Anyway, the 2002 Jeep Grand Cherokee (4-wheel 구동...2006 chyseler pacifica p0700I have tried replacing the 변속기 제어 모듈(TCM) 솔레노이드 and the trans 액슬 입력 속도 센서  still no change car is 고착됨 in limp mode please help...Honda 2001 prelude p0715 and p0700 togetherCode issues are p0715 and p0700 together. I took it to a mechanic and each code he fixed the 엔진 점검등 light would turn off after the job then after driving it both the codes popped back on? He told me not to put more money into the car and to just buy a new 변속기. What I don''t understand ...2005 Jeep Grand Cherokee 4.7. ABS light, 트랙션 컨트롤 light help P0700Any advice for the ABS light, 트랙션 컨트롤 light being on along with the message of service Elec 브레이크 시스템, service  4WD 시스템.  It''s for a  2005 Jeep Grand cherokee 4.7.  I had the ABS 모듈 replaced by my dealership,  they told me my 계기판(클러스터) was bad because message center didn''t work.   T...2004 Dodge Ram 1500 5.7 eng. codes P0700,  P0740Check light stays on all the time. When pulling camper, the red light ( heat trans ) comes on also. Notice no difference in 성능. Getting poorer gas mileage....P0700 IssuesI have', '{"original_en": "### OBD-II Trouble Code Technical Description\nArticle byDale ToalstonASE Certified Technician\nTransmission Control System TCS Malfunction\nThis diagnostic trouble code (DTC) is a generic powertrain code, which means that it applies to OBD-II equipped vehicles. Although generic, the specific repair steps may vary depending on make/model.\n\n### What does that mean?\nMany vehicles have a control module for the automatic transmission called a transmission control module (TCM). The engine control module (ECM) communicates with the TCM to monitor the automatic transmission for faults. If the TCM detects a fault in the automatic transmission and sets a transmission related fault code, the ECM is informed of this also and sets a P0700 in the ECM memory.\nThis illuminates the Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) to let the driver know there is a problem. If this code is present and the MIL (Malfunction Indicator Lamp) is illuminated that basically means there is at least one transmission code set in the TCM''s memory. P0700 is an informational code only. It doesn''t point to a direct fault in the engine, only a general fault in the transmission. More diagnosis is necessary to identify what the transmission fault is. This requires a scan tool that will communicate with the transmission module.SymptomsSymptoms of a P0700 DTC may include:Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) illuminationThe transmission may exhibit drivability problems like slipping, etc.CausesMore often then not, the cause of this code is that there is a transmission problem of some kind. The TCM detected the problem and set a code. P0700 means that a fault code is stored in the TCM. However this doesn''t rule out the possibility of a failed PCM or TCM (unlikely).Possible SolutionsFor a P0700 the only real solution is to acquire a scan tool that will communicate with the transmission control module. Extracting this code from the TCM will be the first step in repairing the fault in the transmission.If the TCM compatible scan tool will not communicate with the Transmission Control Module then that is a good indication that there may be a fault with the TCM itself.Related  DTC DiscussionsRegister now to ask a question (free)2005 Dodge Durango multiple codes set for tranny P0700, P0845, P0731, P0732, P0733I have a 2005 Dodge Durango SXT 4.7L with the 5-45RFE transmission.  It has roughly 138,000 miles on it.  I recently replaced the transmission shift solenoid pack after the truck went into \"limp mode\".  After replacing the solenoid pack I was able to clear the original trouble codes for the solenoid...trans code P0700 2004 pt cruiser gt turboI have a 2004 cruiser gt turbo throwing the code P0700..indicates either a faulty tcm...or solenoid problem in the trans (auto)..car has 144K two owner miles.in better than +9 condition.  When the weather drops below 50 degrees F   the trans does not go into gear until the car has warmed up for almo...2003 dodge caravan code p0700Awhile back my 2003 dodge caravan check engine light went on. Went to autozone to scan, p0700, p1698 and p0500. Van will not go over 50 unless I force accelerate. Changed the in and out speed sensor and a remanufactured TCM from ALL COMPUTER RESOURCES, inc. this TCM gave me more problems, All Comput...2006 Dodge Magnum p0700 and u0100 codesI own a 06 dodge magnum getting a p0700 and u0100 code. Car shuts off 10 times a day ive replaced cam and crankshaft sensors, purge solenoid, plugs, tcm,and pcm and still same stuff. It is a 5.7l rt hemi if anyone has had this problem help me........P0700, no additional codes?Hi all,\nI feel almost guilty posting here; typically I''m very thankful for mechanics and grateful for the work they do. But I just moved to a new state and my jeep starting giving me trouble, so I took it to a local garage (a NAPA AutoCare center). Anyway, the 2002 Jeep Grand Cherokee (4-wheel drive...2006 chyseler pacifica p0700I have tried replacing the TCM solenoid and the trans axle input speed sensor  still no change car is stuck in limp mode please help...Honda 2001 prelude p0715 and p0700 togetherCode issues are p0715 and p0700 together. I took it to a mechanic and each code he fixed the check engine light would turn off after the job then after driving it both the codes popped back on? He told me not to put more money into the car and to just buy a new transmission. What I don''t understand ...2005 Jeep Grand Cherokee 4.7. ABS light, Traction control light help P0700Any advice for the ABS light, traction control light being on along with the message of service Elec Brake system, service  4WD System.  It''s for a  2005 Jeep Grand cherokee 4.7.  I had the ABS module replaced by my dealership,  they told me my cluster was bad because message center didn''t work.   T...2004 Dodge Ram 1500 5.7 eng. codes P0700,  P0740Check light stays on all the time. When pulling camper, the red light ( heat trans ) comes on also. Notice no difference in performance. Getting poorer gas mileage....P0700 IssuesI have ", "manufacturer": "Unknown", "dtc_code": "P0700", "source": "github_dtc_summary"}', '191dbd1a8d3964aacbf69fd201dfafbe253cd26551e71030837eeff89ac0fcc5') ON CONFLICT (content_hash) DO NOTHING;
Article byDon BowmanASE Certified Automotive Tech
시스템 과도하게 희박 at 공회전 (뱅크 1)

### What does that mean?
This diagnostic trouble code (DTC) is a generic 파워트레인 code. It is considered generic because it applies to all makes and models of vehicles (1996-newer), although specific repair steps may be slightly different depending on the model. We have seen this code on Hyundai, Dodge, and other models.
This is an ambiguous code in of itself. It CAN 통신 be a tough code to crack without a diagnostic strategy. During the last two starts, the 엔진 management computer has recognized a problem with the 연료 혼합기 at an 공회전.
It appears that the 연료 혼합기 is 과도하게 희박 (과도하게 much 공기 and not enough 연료) at an 공회전. If you have a 4 실린더 엔진 the "뱅크 1" is meaningless, however, if you have a 6 or 8 실린더 엔진, 뱅크 1 will be on the 측면 with the number one 실린더. CodeP2189is the same code but for 뱅크 #2.There is a laundry list of components that could cause this scenario. For the most part the diagnostic procedure is not difficult -- just time consuming, unless it is one of the first items checked. The strategy dictates that the driveability problems are observed and noted, then 시작 with the most commonly found problems and progress from there.SymptomsWith the wide 범위 of possibilities, the problems listed may and may not be present. But, here is where it is important to pay particular attention to the symptoms observed and make a note as to what and when symptoms appear for diagnostic strategy.Vehicle has a miss at an idleHard to 시작, especially when hotVery irregular idleAdditional codes to pinpoint cause of original P2187 codeWhistling noisesLower turbo 부스트 numbersFuel smellPotential Causes of P2187 DTCFaulty 산소 센서 (전방)Faulty gas 캡 sealLeaky or loose 오일 filler capAir leaking into the 흡기 매니폴드 하류(Downstream) from the Mass Airflow 센서 due to the manifold itself, 진공 hoses off or cracked, 누출 흡기압(MAP) 센서 센서, 누출 at turbo 바이패스 or it''s 열린 채 고착, 전원 브레이크 booster hose, or a 누출 in the 증발 가스 시스템 hoses.Faulty 흡기압(MAP) 센서 sensorEVAP 캐니스터 퍼지 valveFuel 인젝터 leakFuel 압력 regulator faultyLeaks in the 배기 systemFaulty variable 캠샤프트 timingFaulty 엔진 제어 모듈(ECM) (엔진 management computer)Faulty 산소 preheater (전방)Clogged 연료 filterFuel 펌프 wearing out and producing 낮음 압력.Faulty 공기 유량 sensorDiagnostic / Repair StepsYour strategy for locating this problem begins with a 테스트 구동 and observation of any symptoms. The next step is to use a code scanner (available at any auto parts store) and pulling any additional codes.The computer has set a code P2187 stating that the 연료 혼합기 is 희박 at an 공회전. This is the main code, however, any component malfunctioning within this loop that has the potential to cause a 희박 혼합기 will also be set in code.If the 테스트 구동 doesn''t produce any symptoms it is possible that it is not a real code. In other words, the 연료 혼합기 is not 희박 and that the computer or 산소 센서 is responsible for setting the code.Every vehicle has a minimum of two oxygen sensors -- one in 전방 of the 촉매 컨버터 and one after the 컨버터. These sensors 신호 the amount of free oxygen 좌측 in the 배기 after 점화, which determines the 연료 비율. The 전방 센서 is primarily responsible for the 혼합기, the second 센서 behind the 배기 is used for comparison to the 전방 센서 to determine if the 컨버터 is working properly.If a rough 공회전 is present or one of the other symptoms, begin the process with the most likely cause first. Either unmetered 공기 is entering the 흡기 매니폴드 or there is a lack of 연료 압력:Check the 연료 캡 for cracks and sealing and functionLift the hood and make sure the 오일 filler 캡 is tightIf additional codes were present begin with inspecting them firstLook for 공기 leaks starting at the mass airflow 센서. Check the hose or 연결 between the 센서 and the 흡기 매니폴드 all the way to the manifold for cracks or loose connections. Check all 진공 hoses carefully attached to the 흡기 매니폴드, to include the one to the 진공 브레이크 booster. Check the hose to the 흡기압(MAP) 센서 센서 and all hoses to the turbo if so equipped.With the 엔진 running, using a CAN 통신 of carburetor cleaner and spray a small mist around the base of the 흡기 매니폴드 and where the two halves meet if it is a two piece. Spray around the base of the 배기가스 재순환(EGR) for leaks into the manifold. The RPM will increase if a 누출 is located.Check the PCV 밸브 and hose for leaks.Inspect the 연료 injectors for external 연료 leaksInspect the 연료 압력 regulator by pulling off the 진공 hose and shaking it to see if 연료 is present. If so replace it.Shut the 엔진 down and install a 연료 압력 tester on the schrader 밸브 on the 연료 supply rail to the injectors. 시작 the 엔진 and note the 연료 압력 at an 공회전 and once again at 2500 RPM. Compare these fig', '{"original_en": "### OBD-II Trouble Code Technical Description\nArticle byDon BowmanASE Certified Automotive Tech\nSystem Too Lean at Idle (Bank 1)\n\n### What does that mean?\nThis diagnostic trouble code (DTC) is a generic powertrain code. It is considered generic because it applies to all makes and models of vehicles (1996-newer), although specific repair steps may be slightly different depending on the model. We have seen this code on Hyundai, Dodge, and other models.\nThis is an ambiguous code in of itself. It can be a tough code to crack without a diagnostic strategy. During the last two starts, the engine management computer has recognized a problem with the fuel mixture at an idle.\nIt appears that the fuel mixture is too lean (too much air and not enough fuel) at an idle. If you have a 4 cylinder engine the \"Bank 1\" is meaningless, however, if you have a 6 or 8 cylinder engine, Bank 1 will be on the side with the number one cylinder. CodeP2189is the same code but for Bank #2.There is a laundry list of components that could cause this scenario. For the most part the diagnostic procedure is not difficult -- just time consuming, unless it is one of the first items checked. The strategy dictates that the driveability problems are observed and noted, then start with the most commonly found problems and progress from there.SymptomsWith the wide range of possibilities, the problems listed may and may not be present. But, here is where it is important to pay particular attention to the symptoms observed and make a note as to what and when symptoms appear for diagnostic strategy.Vehicle has a miss at an idleHard to start, especially when hotVery irregular idleAdditional codes to pinpoint cause of original P2187 codeWhistling noisesLower turbo boost numbersFuel smellPotential Causes of P2187 DTCFaulty O2 sensor (front)Faulty gas cap sealLeaky or loose oil filler capAir leaking into the intake manifold downstream from the Mass Airflow sensor due to the manifold itself, vacuum hoses off or cracked, leak MAP sensor, Leak at turbo bypass or it''s stuck open, power brake booster hose, or a leak in the EVAP system hoses.Faulty MAP sensorEVAP canister purge valveFuel injector leakFuel pressure regulator faultyLeaks in the exhaust systemFaulty variable camshaft timingFaulty ECM (engine management computer)Faulty O2 preheater (front)Clogged fuel filterFuel pump wearing out and producing low pressure.Faulty mass air flow sensorDiagnostic / Repair StepsYour strategy for locating this problem begins with a test drive and observation of any symptoms. The next step is to use a code scanner (available at any auto parts store) and pulling any additional codes.The computer has set a code P2187 stating that the fuel mixture is lean at an idle. This is the main code, however, any component malfunctioning within this loop that has the potential to cause a lean mixture will also be set in code.If the test drive doesn''t produce any symptoms it is possible that it is not a real code. In other words, the fuel mixture is not lean and that the computer or oxygen sensor is responsible for setting the code.Every vehicle has a minimum of two oxygen sensors -- one in front of the catalytic converter and one after the converter. These sensors signal the amount of free oxygen left in the exhaust after ignition, which determines the fuel ratio. The front sensor is primarily responsible for the mixture, the second sensor behind the exhaust is used for comparison to the front sensor to determine if the converter is working properly.If a rough idle is present or one of the other symptoms, begin the process with the most likely cause first. Either unmetered air is entering the intake manifold or there is a lack of fuel pressure:Check the fuel cap for cracks and sealing and functionLift the hood and make sure the oil filler cap is tightIf additional codes were present begin with inspecting them firstLook for air leaks starting at the mass airflow sensor. Check the hose or connection between the sensor and the intake manifold all the way to the manifold for cracks or loose connections. Check all vacuum hoses carefully attached to the intake manifold, to include the one to the vacuum brake booster. Check the hose to the MAP sensor and all hoses to the turbo if so equipped.With the engine running, using a can of carburetor cleaner and spray a small mist around the base of the intake manifold and where the two halves meet if it is a two piece. Spray around the base of the EGR for leaks into the manifold. The rpm will increase if a leak is located.Check the PCV valve and hose for leaks.Inspect the fuel injectors for external fuel leaksInspect the fuel pressure regulator by pulling off the vacuum hose and shaking it to see if fuel is present. If so replace it.Shut the engine down and install a fuel pressure tester on the schrader valve on the fuel supply rail to the injectors. Start the engine and note the fuel pressure at an idle and once again at 2500 rpm. Compare these fig", "manufacturer": "Unknown", "dtc_code": "P2187", "source": "github_dtc_summary"}', '628bfe3482b762109bb210a20e25fabc8bc9a7768685ff958157a9d8d8b00936') ON CONFLICT (content_hash) DO NOTHING;
